  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#mapping_id_1",
  "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
  "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
  "label": "White people are mapped onto fish",
  "description": "The top text 'when white people learn that' sets up a stereotype that white people are ignorant, and the bottom text 'fish swim in schools' is presented as the punchline. The visual of the naval gunner firing a weapon is used metaphorically to represent the 'attacking' or 'shooting down' of this stereotype. The analogical mapping is that the 'white people' (as a group) are being equated with 'fish' (as a group) in the context of the stereotype, and the firing of the weapon symbolizes the aggressive dismissal of this ignorance. The visual material (naval gunner firing) is mapped onto the textual material (the stereotype about white people being ignorant of fish behavior).",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
